            scheme involves more work (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProductInducesPerturbativeSMatrix"}
            below).
          #NotationForTimeOrderedProductsAsGeneralizedFunctions.num_remark
            %h6#remark_15 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
                as
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+functions"} generalized functions
            %p
              It is convenient (as in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#EpsteinGlaser73"} Epstein-Glaser 73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProduct"}
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
              (hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator-valued+distributions"} operator-valued distributions
              if we were to choose a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operators"} linear operators
              on a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+functions"} generalized functions
              depending on spacetime points:
            %p If
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
