            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              The axiom “perturbation” of the S-matrix is immediate from the axioms “perturbation” and “normalization” of the time-ordered products. What requires proof is that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+additivity"} causal additivity
              of the S-matrix follows from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+factorization"} causal factorization
              property of the time-ordered products.
            %p
              Notice that also the weaker
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+factorization"} causal factorization
              property of the S-matrix (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DysonCausalFactorization"}
            %p
              But
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+additivity"} causal additivity
              is stronger. It is remarkable that this, too, follows from just the time-ordering (
              %a{:href => "S-matrix#EpsteinGlaser73"}> Epstein-Glaser 73, around (73)
              ):
