                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1, A_2 \in PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})_{mc}[ [ \hbar, g, j] ]
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+polynomial+observables"} microcausal polynomial observables
              with disjoint spacetime support the star product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 \star_F A_2
              is well-defined and satisfies causal factorization.
            %p
              Consider two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partitions+of+unity"} partitions of unity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
