            %h6#proof_17 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"}
              the contributions to the S-matrix away from coinciding interaction points are given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
              induced by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FeynmanPerturbationSeriesAwayFromCoincidingPoints"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
              are given this way. Moreover the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropagatorStarProduct"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
              and then multiplying all resulting terms with the pointwise product of observables. This implies the claim by the nature of the combinatorial factor in the definition of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
              (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FeynmanPerturbationSeriesAwayFromCoincidingPoints"}
          #InPerturbationTheoryActionEffective.num_defn
            %h6#definition_22 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+action"}> effective action
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
